## 2. Reference Practices and Evaluation Criteria

The assessment uses widely adopted industry principles as a measurement framework. It is an engineering checklist, not a formal certification.

| Reference | Application |
|---|---|
| Test Pyramid (Fowler, Google Testing Blog) | Many unit tests, fewer widget tests, few integration tests |
| FIRST (Fast, Isolated, Repeatable, Self-validating, Timely) | Mocked dependencies; no real network or storage in unit tests |
| ISTQB test levels and independence | Cubit logic separated from UI; UI separated from data |
| Flutter/Bloc community practice | `bloc_test`, `mocktail`, golden testing |
| CI maturity (basic quality gate) | PR/push → format → analyze → test → coverage |
| Clean Architecture testability | Use cases and repositories mockable through interfaces or injection |

